title: Align Tally::approval() with VoteTally trait semantics
doc:
- audience: Todo
  description: |-
    # Description

    Aligns `Tally::approval()` in `pallet-conviction-voting` with the `VoteTally` trait semantics by
    returning `Perbill::zero()` when no aye or nay votes have been cast. This makes the production
    implementation consistent with the existing behavior in the `pallet-referenda` test mock
    (`substrate/frame/referenda/src/mock.rs:263-269`).

    Additionally, the `VoteTally::approval()` trait doc in `frame-support` is updated to explicitly
    document the expected return value when no votes have been cast, preventing future implementors
    from diverging on this behavior.

    ## Integration

    Downstream projects that implement `VoteTally::approval()` should ensure they handle the case where
    no votes have been cast (i.e. `ayes + nays == 0`) by returning `Perbill::zero()`, as now documented
    in the trait definition.

    No breaking changes to the public API. The `Tally` struct and its fields remain unchanged.

    ## Review Notes

    Two changes:

    **1. Trait documentation** (`substrate/frame/support/src/traits/voting.rs`):

    ```diff
    -    /// Returns the approval ratio (positive to total votes) for the tally.
    +    /// Returns the approval ratio (positive to total votes) for the tally and returns 0% (`Perbill::zero()`)
    +    /// if no votes have been cast (i.e. `ayes + nays == 0`).
         fn approval(&self, class: Class) -> Perbill;
    ```

    **2. Implementation fix** (`substrate/frame/conviction-voting/src/types.rs`):

    ```diff
     fn approval(&self, _: Class) -> Perbill {
    -    Perbill::from_rational(self.ayes, self.ayes.saturating_add(self.nays))
    +    let total = self.ayes.saturating_add(self.nays);
    +    if total.is_zero() {
    +        Perbill::zero()
    +    } else {
    +        Perbill::from_rational(self.ayes, total)
    +    }
     }
    ```

    A new test `empty_tally_approval_is_zero` is added covering four scenarios:

    | Scenario    | ayes | nays | Expected approval |
    |-------------|------|------|-------------------|
    | No votes    | 0    | 0    | 0%                |
    | Only ayes   | 10   | 0    | 100%              |
    | Only nays   | 0    | 10   | 0%                |
    | Mixed votes | 3    | 7    | 30%               |

    All 25 existing `pallet-conviction-voting` tests continue to pass with no regressions.

    # Checklist

    * [x] My PR includes a detailed description as outlined in the "Description" and its two subsections above.
    * [x] My PR follows the [labeling requirements](
    https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/blob/master/docs/contributor/CONTRIBUTING.md#Process
    ) of this project (at minimum one label for `T` required)
    * [x] I have made corresponding changes to the documentation (if applicable)
    * [x] I have added tests that prove my fix is effective or that my feature works (if applicable)
crates:
- name: pallet-conviction-voting
  bump: major
- name: frame-support
  bump: major
